          "teaching": {
            "prerequisite_note": "Before starting: use find to search live folders, cat to read text and cp to copy a file. You can revisit those earlier lessons. Here you will learn why a saved filename search can disagree with the files that exist now.",
            "concepts": [
              {
                "title": "A fast search can use yesterday\u2019s names",
                "text": "find walks the supplied virtual folders now. locate searches a separate saved list of names. A deleted or renamed file can still appear in that list, and a new file can be missing. Reading a returned path with cat checks the file\u2019s actual contents."
              },
              {
                "title": "Exclusions affect the next rebuild",
                "text": "The native editor changes the PRUNEPATHS setting: quoted absolute folders whose contents should be skipped. A folder\u2019s own name may remain listed; its descendants are excluded. An exact archive exclusion does not hide the separate archives folder. Save configuration applies the text; it does not update the saved list. Real system defaults commonly use /etc/updatedb.conf. Here you edit the supplied private file, so this exercise affects only its private index."
              },
              {
                "title": "Rebuild explicitly, then verify",
                "text": "updatedb -l 0 -o DATABASE -U ROOT --config-file CONFIG builds this activity\u2019s private index. Each path is supplied by the lesson. A successful rebuild prints nothing. locate -e -d DATABASE TEXT filters saved names by current existence; it does not add missing names or refresh the index."
              },
              {
                "title": "A filename is not proof of the right document",
                "text": "Use cat PATH to read a file and cp SOURCE DEST to copy it. Read the current and archive files before copying. The assignment checks the saved exclusions, a fresh index and the actual handover contents, while preserving everything else. All commands and files stay inside the simulator; this private-index exercise does not reproduce system-wide access or visibility rules."
              }
            ],
            "description": "Separate worked example: the /gallery index still names guide-old.txt, and its saved configuration wrongly excludes current. Repair the configuration, rebuild, and hand over the current guide. The three stages below explain what each action changes.",
            "worked": [
              {
                "title": "Save the intended exclusions",
                "explanation": "Keep archive excluded; remove current from PRUNEPATHS. Save applies this text but does not rebuild saved names.",
                "step": {
                  "kind": "SaveConfig",
                  "text": "PRUNEPATHS = \"/gallery/archive\"\n"
                }
              },
              {
                "title": "Refresh the private saved names",
                "explanation": "Run updatedb with the supplied private output, root and configuration. A successful rebuild is quiet; locate will now use the refreshed names.",
                "step": {
                  "kind": "Command",
                  "input": "updatedb -l 0 -o /indexes/demo.db -U /gallery --config-file /practice/index.conf"
                }
              },
              {
                "title": "Copy the current document",
                "explanation": "Read the current file, then copy it to the handover. The archived file has the same name but different contents.",
                "step": {
                  "kind": "Command",
                  "input": "cp /gallery/current/guide.txt /practice/handover.txt"
                }
              }
            ],
            "try_steps": [
              {
                "title": "Compare saved names with live files",
                "explanation": "Insert and run this query. Before your first rebuild, the saved index lists guide-old.txt. Then type find /gallery -name \"guide*.txt\" to compare with live files. After rebuilding, repeat the query to observe the change.",
                "step": {
                  "kind": "Command",
                  "input": "locate -d /indexes/demo.db guide"
                }
              },
              {
                "title": "Save the narrower exclusion",
                "explanation": "Fill this practice configuration, then choose Save configuration. Repeat locate: saving alone does not change the saved names.",
                "step": {
                  "kind": "SaveConfig",
                  "text": "PRUNEPATHS = \"/gallery/archive\"\n"
                }
              },
              {
                "title": "Rebuild, then compare",
                "explanation": "With archive-only exclusions saved, run the explicit rebuild and repeat locate. Expected after rebuilding: guide.txt replaces guide-old.txt, while /gallery/archive/guide.txt remains excluded.",
                "step": {
                  "kind": "Command",
                  "input": "updatedb -l 0 -o /indexes/demo.db -U /gallery --config-file /practice/index.conf"
                }
              },
              {
                "title": "Prepare and check the handover",
                "explanation": "Copy the current file, then choose Check practice. Compare cat /practice/handover.txt with cat /gallery/current/guide.txt.",
                "step": {
